# RootneX CyberWatch

RootneX CyberWatch is a Windows command-line toolkit designed to simplify day-to-day system administration, network diagnostics, and security monitoring. It combines multiple administrative utilities into a single interactive console, allowing IT professionals to monitor system performance, troubleshoot network connectivity, inspect security events, and perform maintenance tasks from one place.

## Features

- Monitor CPU, Memory, Disk, Services, and System Uptime
- Diagnose network issues using Ping, Traceroute, DNS Lookup, and Port Scanning
- Review Windows Firewall configuration and active rules
- Analyze Event Logs and detect failed login attempts
- Monitor remote clients and perform administrative actions
- Generate system, network, and security reports
- Perform maintenance tasks such as DNS cache flushing and network repair
- Access common Windows administrative commands through a unified interface

## Technologies

- Batch Script
- Windows Command Prompt (CMD)
- PowerShell
- Windows Networking Utilities
- WMIC
- Netsh
- Netstat

## Getting Started

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/ahaliMz/CyberWatch.git
```

Run the application with administrative privileges:

```bash
cd CyberWatch
src\cyberwatch.bat
```

